\ Spitfire: the raid and the fighting. A model is a sketch in its own terms —
\ metres right, up and forward of its centre — drawn by carrying its points
\ through one more matrix product, from its own terms into the ground's, on
\ their way into the eye's. The Ju 88 A-4 and the He 111 H are built to their
\ published spans and lengths (20.08 m by 14.36 m, 22.60 m by 16.40 m), the
\ rest of their proportions estimated from drawings: fuselages of eight-sided
\ rings, the glazing, the gun positions and gondolas, tapered wings with
\ their hinge lines, round nacelles with three-blade propellers, the tail
\ surfaces with theirs, and the crosses.
\
\ A raid is bombers in vics of three, each following the one ahead of it: the
\ leader of each vic flies to the target at its speed and height, the others
\ station off its wings and behind; over the target they bomb, then turn for
\ home. An escort of Bf 110s fights until the bombers have bombed: each
\ takes the nearest Spitfire, the player's or the squadron's, breaks toward
\ it when it is behind, turns onto it within 3 km with the lead its rounds
\ need, and otherwise rejoins the bombers. The squadron's other Spitfires
\ break hard from a Bf 110 behind them and otherwise attack the nearest of
\ the raid. The turns are the Spitfire Mk I's 360° in 19 s at 12,000 ft
\ (RAE, published) and the Bf 110 C's 23.2 s, derived from it by the square
\ root of the wing loadings (175 kg/m² against 117), the wings taken to
\ reach the same greatest lift. Everything about the guns is gunnery.telic's;
\ an aircraft whose hits pass its strength smokes, rolls over and falls.

0x908070 constant smoke-colour

\ the Luftwaffe's finish of 1939 to 1941: the upper surfaces in RLM 70 and 71, drawn as one dark green between them, the under surfaces RLM 65 light blue, the crosses black over white; the target drogue's canvas; HMS Glorious's grey and her flight deck's (every shade an estimate)
0x3a4232 constant luftwaffe-upper-colour
0x93a8b8 constant luftwaffe-under-colour
0x141414 constant cross-black-colour
0xe6e6e0 constant cross-white-colour
0xd8d2c0 constant canvas-colour
0x7c848a constant carrier-grey-colour
0x5c5a52 constant flight-deck-colour

\ an engine on each wing: the nacelle as rings of six from its round cowling back past the wing, the propeller and its disc before it 0.15 m ahead of the face, the spinner of six sides through [ ahead-of-face radius ] pairs, six exhaust stubs down each side of the cowling; the spinner and the hub on the cowling face's centre; the stations are [ along radius ] from the cowling's face, or [ along half-width half-height drop ] for a nacelle deeper than it is wide, the drop added to the lift
\ the Jumo 211's spinner, a blunt dome, as [ ahead-of-face radius ] pairs (measured on the He 111 from a side profile)
[ [ 0.05 0.4 ] [ 0.15 0.4 ] [ 0.35 0.37 ] [ 0.5 0.28 ] [ 0.6 0.16 ] [ 0.65 0.05 ] ] constant bomber-spinner

: sketch-engines ( sketch out lift face stations propeller-radius spinner-profile -- )
	| sketch out lift face stations propeller-radius spinner-profile |
	stations ( station | station size 2 > if [ station first face + station second station 2 @i station 3 @i lift + ] else [ station first face + station second station second lift ] then ) map to rings
	stations second second to cowling
	rings first 3 @i to axis-height
	face 0.15 + to hub-along
	spinner-profile ( place | [ face place first + place second place second axis-height ] ) map to spinner
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ out side * 0 0 ] to centre
		sketch rings centre 6 sketch-body
		sketch spinner centre 6 sketch-body
		centre [ 0 axis-height hub-along ] v+ to hub
		sketch hub propeller-radius sketch-propeller
		sketch hub propeller-radius sketch-propeller-disc
		[ -1 1 ] ( flank |
			0 6 1 do stub
				face 0.3 - stub 0.22 * - to along
				[ out side * flank cowling * + lift 0.15 + along ] to root
				sketch [ root root [ flank 0.1 * -0.03 -0.1 ] v+ ] sketch-path
			loop
		) each
	) each ;

\ the Balkenkreuz's outline as [ across up ] pairs about its middle: a cross reaching a distance each way, its arms a half-width each side of their middle lines
: cross-pairs ( reach bar -- pairs )
	| reach bar |
	[ [ bar reach ] [ bar bar ] [ reach bar ] [ reach bar negate ] [ bar bar negate ] [ bar reach negate ]
	  [ bar negate reach negate ] [ bar negate bar negate ] [ reach negate bar negate ] [ reach negate bar ] [ bar negate bar ] [ bar negate reach ] ] ;

\ the Balkenkreuz painted on a flat surface facing an outward direction, by the Luftwaffe's rule: a black cross a length long, its arms a quarter as wide; a white angle a flank wide along each side of each arm, ending flush with the arm's end, drawn as a white cross as long under the black
: sketch-cross ( sketch centre across up outward size flank -- )
	| sketch centre across up outward size flank |
	size 2 / to reach
	reach 4 / to bar
	[ [ 0.004 bar flank + cross-white-colour ] [ 0.008 bar cross-black-colour ] ] ( layer |
		layer spread to colour to half-width to proud
		centre outward proud v* v+ to middle
		sketch reach half-width cross-pairs ( pair | middle across pair first v* v+ up pair second v* v+ ) map
		centre outward v- colour sketch-painted-plate
	) each ;

\ the Balkenkreuz on a side of a body of rings, on the skin, centred on the side's ridge at a station: nine tenths as long as the height between the shoulders 45° above and below the ridge where its rear end lies, the white angles an eighth of its length wide, as on the fuselage by the rule; each colour cut at the ridge, the half above it on the face above, the half below on the face below
: sketch-body-cross ( sketch rings along side -- )
	| sketch rings along side |
	rings along body-ring-at 2 @i 0.5 sqrt * 2 * 0.9 * to size
	rings along size 2 / - body-ring-at 2 @i 0.5 sqrt * 2 * 0.9 * to size
	rings along body-ring-at 3 @i to lift
	size 2 / to reach
	reach 4 / to bar
	[ [ 0.01 bar size 8 / + cross-white-colour ] [ 0.02 bar cross-black-colour ] ] ( layer |
		layer spread to colour to half-width to proud
		[ 1 -1 ] ( keep |
			reach half-width cross-pairs 1 0 keep clip-pairs
			( pair | rings along pair first + lift pair second + side proud body-side-point ) map to corners
			sketch corners [ 0 lift along ] colour sketch-painted-plate
		) each
	) each ;

\ the crosses: on each upper wing at a distance out, a length long with the upper surface's narrow white angles, a twentieth of the length (the Bf 109's 50 mm on 1000 mm), and on each side of the fuselage at a station
: sketch-crosses ( sketch rings wing-out wing-along wing-height wing-size side-along -- )
	| sketch rings wing-out wing-along wing-height wing-size side-along |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		sketch [ wing-out side * wing-height wing-along ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 0 1 ] [ 0 1 0 ] wing-size wing-size 20 / sketch-cross
		sketch rings side-along side sketch-body-cross
	) each ;

\ the swastika on a fin, as the Luftwaffe painted it from 1939: black with a thin white border, standing on a corner, its arms turning clockwise as seen from the side it is painted on; laid out on a grid of five by five cells, a bar each way through the middle and a hook at the end of each arm, each a rectangle of cells [ left bottom right top ]; the border a fifth of a cell (an estimate)
[ [ 2 0 3 5 ] [ 0 2 5 3 ] [ 3 4 5 5 ] [ 4 0 5 2 ] [ 0 0 2 1 ] [ 0 3 1 5 ] ] constant swastika-cells
0.2 constant swastika-border

\ the swastika's pieces, each a rectangle of cells widened by a margin, as points on a surface: its middle, its upward direction, its width, the direction to the right as seen from outside
: swastika-pieces ( centre right up size margin -- pieces )
	| centre right up size margin |
	size 5 / to cell
	swastika-cells ( piece |
		piece spread to top to right-edge to bottom to left-edge
		[ [ left-edge margin - bottom margin - ] [ right-edge margin + bottom margin - ] [ right-edge margin + top margin + ] [ left-edge margin - top margin + ] ]
		( corner |
			corner first 2.5 - cell * to u
			corner second 2.5 - cell * to v
			centre right u v - 2 sqrt / v* v+ up u v + 2 sqrt / v* v+
		) map
	) map ;

\ a swastika painted on a surface facing an outward direction: the white pieces widened by the border, then the black over them
: sketch-swastika ( sketch centre up outward size -- )
	| sketch centre up outward size |
	outward up v-cross to right
	centre outward 0.004 v* v+ right up size swastika-border swastika-pieces ( piece | sketch piece centre outward v- cross-white-colour sketch-painted-plate ) each
	centre outward 0.008 v* v+ right up size 0 swastika-pieces ( piece | sketch piece centre outward v- cross-black-colour sketch-painted-plate ) each ;

\ the swastikas on a fin a distance out, its outline as [ along up ] points: at the outline's middle, a third as wide as the outline is tall or long, the lesser; on the fin's outer side, or on both sides of a fin on the centre line
: sketch-fin-swastikas ( sketch out outline -- )
	| sketch out outline |
	outline outline-middle spread to middle-up to middle-along
	outline ( pair | pair first ) map to alongs
	outline ( pair | pair second ) map to ups
	alongs alongs first ' max2 reduce alongs alongs first ' min2 reduce - to length
	ups ups first ' max2 reduce ups ups first ' min2 reduce - to height
	length height min2 3 / to size
	out 0 = if [ -1 1 ] else [ out 0 > if 1 else -1 then ] then ( side |
		sketch [ out middle-up middle-along ] [ 0 1 0 ] [ side 0 0 ] size sketch-swastika
	) each ;

\ glass's colour: a dark blue-grey drawn unlit, 0x1000000 set, so it keeps one tone toward the sun or away from it (an estimate)
0x1788c98 constant glass-colour

\ a gunner's hood of glass on a body of rings, rounded and open at its rear: at each station [ along height half-width ] an arch of five points from the skin on one side over the top to the skin on the other, its height above the body's top, its half-width where it meets the skin, the skin there on the body's top face; glass between each arch and the next, facing away from a point below them inside the body; the arches and the lines joining them the frames
: sketch-gun-hood ( sketch rings stations -- )
	| sketch rings stations |
	stations ( station |
		station spread to half-width to height to along
		rings along body-ring-at spread to lift to half-height to body-half-width drop
		[ 0 5 1 do k
			k 45 * 90 - PI 180 / * to angle
			angle sin half-width * to across
			lift half-height + across abs body-half-width 0.5 sqrt * / 1 0.5 sqrt - * half-height * - to skin
			[ across skin angle cos height * + along ]
		loop ] to arch
		sketch arch sketch-points to indices
		sketch indices join-path
		indices
	) map to arches
	0 arches size 1- 1 do k
		arches k @i to front
		arches k 1+ @i to back
		stations k @i first stations k 1+ @i first + 2 / to middle
		[ 0 rings middle body-top 0.3 - middle ] to inside
		0 5 1 do corner
			sketch front corner @i back corner @i sketch-edge
		loop
		0 4 1 do corner
			sketch [ front corner @i front corner 1+ @i back corner 1+ @i back corner @i ] inside glass-colour sketch-painted-face
		loop
	loop ;

\ the Ju 88 A-4: a fuselage of rings, its nose a dome of small panes back to its frame, then a band of skin to the windscreen; the canopy over the crew's compartment, a hood of glass with its frames, and the two rear guns; the ventral gondola, half the fuselage's width, hung under the cockpit 0.23 m to starboard, in the under colour, with its front window, two side windows each side, its glazed rear and its gun; the aerial from a mast on the canopy to the fin; tapered wings with rounded tips and the flaps' and ailerons' hinge line; the Jumo 211s in round cowlings with three-blade propellers; the tailplane, elevators, fin and rudder; the crosses, sized to fit their surfaces, and the swastikas on the fins; the glazing in glass's colour; the under colour on the bottom faces only. The span and length are published; the side outline is measured from a side painting and the gondola's width and offset from a front view, both scaled to them; every other figure is an estimate
: junkers-88 ( -- model )
	new-model-sketch luftwaffe-under-colour :under-colour ! 0.5 :under-turn ! to model
	model@faces size to first-face
	[ [ 7.1 0.08 0.1 0.02 ] [ 7.05 0.16 0.185 0.015 ] [ 6.95 0.28 0.315 0.055 ] [ 6.85 0.36 0.39 0.08 ] [ 6.7 0.44 0.455 0.095 ] [ 6.46 0.52 0.545 0.125 ]
	  [ 6.1 0.6 0.675 0.205 ] [ 3.8 0.64 0.71 0.24 ] [ 1.5 0.64 0.69 0.31 ]
	  [ -1.5 0.58 0.6 0.4 ] [ -4.0 0.44 0.49 0.46 ] [ -6.6 0.24 0.335 0.515 ] [ -7.05 0.08 0.1 0.45 ] ] to rings
	model rings [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	[ 0 40 1 do k first-face k + loop first-face 96 + ] ( face | model@faces face @i glass-colour add-last! drop ) each
	[ 0.23 0 0 ] to gondola-centre
	[ [ 6.55 0.1 0.1 -0.4 ] [ 6.45 0.2 0.16 -0.46 ] [ 6.3 0.26 0.205 -0.505 ] [ 6.0 0.29 0.24 -0.54 ] [ 5.4 0.29 0.29 -0.59 ]
	  [ 4.6 0.29 0.26 -0.56 ] [ 4.2 0.27 0.23 -0.53 ] [ 3.9 0.23 0.175 -0.475 ] ] to gondola
	model@faces size to gondola-first-face
	model gondola gondola-centre 8 sketch-body
	0 58 1 do k
		model@faces gondola-first-face k + @i k 8 < k 55 > or if glass-colour else luftwaffe-under-colour then add-last! drop
	loop
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ 5.1 4.7 ] ( middle |
			[ [ middle 0.08 + -0.56 ] [ middle 0.08 - -0.56 ] [ middle 0.08 - -0.42 ] [ middle 0.08 + -0.42 ] ]
			( place | gondola place spread side 0.01 body-side-point gondola-centre v+ ) map to pane
			model pane gondola-centre [ 0 -0.6 middle ] v+ glass-colour sketch-painted-plate
		) each
	) each
	model rings [ [ 6.17 0.06 0.4 ] [ 6.0 0.3 0.44 ] [ 5.9 0.37 0.44 ] [ 5.3 0.35 0.44 ] [ 4.8 0.33 0.44 ] [ 4.27 0.32 0.44 ] [ 3.8 0.05 0.36 ] ] sketch-gun-hood
	[ -1 1 ] ( side | model [ side 0.15 * 1.1 3.9 ] [ side 0.15 * 1.15 3.1 ] 0.05 model-ink sketch-rod ) each
	model [ 0.23 -0.6 3.9 ] [ 0.23 -0.85 3.2 ] 0.06 model-ink sketch-rod
	model [ [ 0.45 4.33 ] [ 3.4 4.25 ] [ 6.2 3.83 ] [ 9.1 3.33 ] [ 9.55 3.2 ] [ 9.9 2.9 ] [ 10.04 2.6 ] [ 9.9 2.25 ] [ 9.6 2.04 ] [ 9.1 1.95 ] [ 5.2 1.3 ] [ 0.45 0.68 ] ]
		[ [ [ 3.2 1.25 ] [ 9.3 2.3 ] ] [ [ 4.9 1.31 ] [ 4.9 1.6 ] ] ] 0.06 0 sketch-surface
	model 2.72 0.3 6.0 [ [ 0 0.62 ] [ -0.6 0.7 ] [ -2.7 0.6 ] [ -4.0 0.45 ] [ -5.1 0 ] ] 1.7 bomber-spinner sketch-engines
	model [ [ 0.2 -4.13 ] [ 1.91 -4.41 ] [ 3.17 -4.66 ] [ 3.53 -4.81 ] [ 3.68 -5.17 ] [ 3.58 -5.44 ] [ 3.43 -5.54 ] [ 2.17 -5.77 ] [ 0.2 -5.97 ] ]
