	model luftwaffe-upper-colour sketch>object ;

\ the Bf 110 C: a slim fuselage of eight rings; the long glazed canopy over the pilot and the gunner, its frames and the gunner's MG 15; the four MG 17s in the nose and the two MG FF cannon under it; tapered wings with the hinge line; the DB 601s in slim nacelles with three-blade propellers; the tailplane and the twin fins at its tips; the crosses, sized to fit their surfaces, and the swastikas on the fins; the glazing in glass's colour. The span, length and height are published (16.25 m, 12.1 m, 3.5 m); every other figure is an estimate from drawings
