	    :briefing "PHOTOGRAPH THE TIRPITZ IN FAETTENFJORD FROM 30,000 FT AND LAND WITH THE FILM. YOU ARE UNARMED. THE TARGET'S BEARING AND DISTANCE ARE IN THE STRIP BELOW THE PANEL. RUN THE CAMERAS (C) OVER HER: THE SPLIT PAIR TAKES OVERLAPPING FRAMES, 125 TO A MAGAZINE. THE HEAVY FLAK REACHES ABOUT 26,000 FT AND CANNOT FOLLOW AN AIRCRAFT CROSSING THE SKY FAST; THE LIGHT FLAK IS DANGEROUS LOW DOWN. T RUNS TIME FASTER. ONCE LANDED, V DEVELOPS THE FILM FOR REVIEW." }
	  { :name "FLYING LESSON AT TURNHOUSE"
	    :story [ "AN INSTRUCTOR IN THE BACK SEAT TALKS YOU THROUGH"
